window.WIKI_SEARCH_INDEX = [{"slug":"mediography","title":"Mediografia","book":"book1","excerpt":"As obras que inspiraram Stonetop: jogos, blogs, livros, filmes, séries e podcasts, com uma ressalva sobre seus criadores.","text":"Mediografia\n Influências diretas de jogo\n The following works directly inspired Stonetop 's mechanics, techniques, setting, themes, and approach to information design.\n Dungeon World , Adam Koebel & Sage LaTorra, Sage Kobold Productions, 2012\n Apocalypse World , D. Vincent Baker & Meguey Baker, lumpley games, 2010\n Storming the Wizard's Tower , D. Vincent Baker, unpublished, 2008\n Dungeons & Dragons (4th Edition), Rob Heinsoo, Andy Collins, and James Wyatt; Wizards of the Coast, 2008\n Blades in the Dark , John Harper, Evil Hat Productions, 2017\n Beyond the Wall and Other Adventures , John Cocking & Peter S. Williams, Flatland Games, 2013\n The Perilous Wilds , Jason Lutes, Lampblack & Brimstone, 2016\n 20 Dungeon Starters , Marshall Miller & Mark Tygart, Lampblack & Brimstone, 2016\n Trilemma Adventures , Michael Prescott, Trilemma Adventures, 2019\n Ars Magica , Mark Rein-Hagen & Jonathan Tweet, Lion Rampant Games, 1987\n Blogs\n You can find a lot of writing about Stonetop and its development at Jeremy's blog, Spouting Lore (2018-2023). Additionally, the following essays and series either influenced techniques and approaches presented in this game or demonstrate the game in action.\n \" Apocalypse World : Crossing the Line ,\" John Harper, The Mighty Atom , 2010\n \" Paint the Scene ,\" Jason Cordova, The Gauntlet Blog , 2018\n \" The 7-3-1 Technique ,\" Jason Cordova, The Gauntlet Blog , 2018\n \" A 16 HP Dragon \", Stras Acimovic, republicado por Sage LaTorra, Latorra.org, 2012\n \" Powered by the Apocalypse \" (12-part series), D. Vincent Baker, lumpley games , 2019-2025\n A Collection of Unmitigated Pedantry , Bret Devereaux, 2019-present (especially the \" Practical Polytheism \" series and the \" Iron, How Did They Make It? \" series)\n \" Xandering the Dungeon ,\" Justin Alexander, The Alexandrian , 2010\n \" Dungeon Checklist \", Arnold K., Goblin Punch \n \" PTFO: Stonetop \" (solo actual-play series), SGH, PTFO on Substack, 2022-present\n Referências\n There's no one thing you can point at and say \" Stonetop is just like this.\" But here's some stuff that you might look to for vibes.\n Barbarians (série de TV), Andreas Heckmann et al, Gaumont Germany, 2020-2022\n The Bear and the Nightingale (book; and to a lesser extent the whole Winternight trilogy), Katherine Arden, Del Rey, 2017\n The Chronicles of Prydain (book series), Lloyd Alexander; Holt, Reinhart, and Winston; 1964-1968\n The Dark is Rising Sequence (book series), Susan Cooper, Random House, 1965-1977\n The Demon Cycle (book series), Peter V. Brett, Penguin Random House, 2010-2017\n Farseer (trilogia de livros), Robin Hobb, Spectra, 1995-1997\n The First Law (série de livros), Joe Abercrombie, Orbit Books, 2006-presente\n O Hobbit (livro), J.R.R. Tolkien, George Allen & Unwin, 1937\n King of Dragon Pass (video game), David Dunham, A Sharp, 1999 (or anything else related to the Glorantha setting by Greg Stafford (so I'm told))\n The Last Kingdom (TV series), Stephen Butchard et al, Carnival Film and Television, 2015-2017\n Nausicaä of the Valley of the Wind (film), Hayao Miyazaki, Studio Ghibli, 1984\n Northlanders (série de quadrinhos), Brian Wood, Vertigo, 2008-2012\n Princesa Mononoke (filme), Hayao Miyazaki, Studio Ghibli, 1984\n Redwall (série de livros), Brian Jacques, Penguin Books, 1986-2011\n Rome (série de TV), John Milius et al, HBO, 2005-2007\n The Secret of Kells (film), Tomm Moore & Nora Twomey, Les Armateurs, 2009\n The Sharing Knife (book series), Lois McMaster Bujold, HarperCollins, 2006-2019\n Shattered Sea (trilogia de livros) Joe Abercrombie, Del Rey, 2014-2015\n Vikings (série de TV), Michael Hirst, TM Productions et al, 2013-2021\n Um Mago de Terramar (livro), Ursula K. Le Guin, Parnassus Press, 1968\n The Driftless region of Wisconsin , and Texas Hill Country \n E também...\n The following influenced or inspired certain specific elements of Stonetop , or resonate strongly with some of its themes. Maybe they'll inspire you, too.\n At the Mountains of Madness (novella), H.P. Lovecraft, Astounding Stories , 1936 (and other stories by Lovecraft)\n The Black Company (série de livros), Glen Cook, 1984-presente, Tor Fantasy\n Black Spot (série de TV), Mathieu Missoffe, Ego Productions et al, 2017-2019\n Chronos (film), Guillermo del Toro, Fondo de Fomento Cinematográfico et al, 1992\n The \"Conan\" stories (books and adaptations); Robert E. Howard, L. Sprague de Camp, and Lin Carter; various publishers, 1950-1977 (especially \" Red Nails \")\n Deadwood (série de TV), David Milch, Roscoe Productions et al, 2004-2006\n Discern Realities (podcast), Jason Cordova & David LaFrieniere, The Gauntlet, 2015-2019\n Gentleman Bastard (série de livros), Scott Lynch, Bantam Books, 2006-2013\n Gladiador (filme), Ridley Scott, DreamWorks Pictures et al, 2000\n Heart Shaped Box (livro), Joe Hill, William Morrow, 2007\n Hillfolk (RPG), Robin Laws, Pelgrane Press, 2013\n Marcas da Violência (filme), David Cronenberg, BenderSpink et al, 2005\n Jonathan Strange and Mr Norrell (book), Susanna Clarke, Bloomsbury, 2004\n Legacy: Life Among the Ruins (RPG), Minerva McJanda, UFO Press, 2015\n Little House on the Prairie (book series), Laura Ingalls Wilder, Harper & Brothers, 1932-1971\n Low Country (álbum), The Sword, Razor & Tie, 2016\n The Magnus Archives (podcast), Jonathan Simms & Alexander J. Newall, Rusty Quill, 2016-2021\n Mouse Guard (comic book series), David Petersen, Archaia Studios Press, 2006-present\n Monster Man (podcast), James Holloway, 2018-presente\n No Country for Old Kobolds (RPG), Steve Wallace, Steve Wallace Art, 2016\n Old Gods of Appalachia (podcast), Steve Shell & Cam Collins, Deepnerd Media, 2019-present\n O Labirinto do Fauno (filme, 2006), Guillermo del Toro, Estudios Picasso et al, 2006\n Predador: A Caçada (filme), Dan Trachtenberg, 20th Century Studios et al, 2022\n The Revenant (film), Alejandro González Iñárritu, Regency Enterprises et al, 2015\n O Ritual (filme), David Bruckner, The Imaginarium, 2017\n Sagas of the Icelanders (RPG), Gregor Vuga, 2013\n O Segredo de NIMH (filme), Don Bluth, United Artists, 1982\n Under Hollow Hills (RPG), Meguey Baker & D. Vincent Baker, lumpley games, 2021\n The Wardstone Chronicles (book series), Joseph Delaney, Greenwillow Books, 2004-2013\n Caveat emptor\n Tudo o que está acima é relevante e potencialmente útil como inspiração, mas não é necessariamente tudo bom.\n And some of the creators held and espoused hurtful beliefs, which permeates their work. Others have done or been accused of terrible things. People, like art and our consumption of it, are complicated.","local":1}];
